  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Bright red blood with bowel movements for about three months, with narrower stools, urgency, a feeling of incomplete emptying, and a firm, ulcerated mass felt on the back wall of the lower rectum at about 5 cm from the anal verge: a rectal cancer must be confirmed or excluded. Colonoscopy with biopsy booked this week</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
