  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Iron deficiency anemia from chronic rectal blood loss: hemoglobin 11.0 g/dL, MCV 77 fL, ferritin 9 ng/mL, with tiredness</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D50.0</td><td>S — Synthetic finding anchored to the documented fatigue at the end of the 1952 season.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Adenocarcinoma of the low rectum, mismatch repair deficient (loss of MSH2 and MSH6; microsatellite instability high), cT3bN1M0 (stage IIIB) on pelvic MRI, lower edge 4 cm from the anal verge and about 1 cm above the anorectal junction, mesorectal fascia clear, no extramural venous invasion; CEA 5.8 ng/mL; synthetic modern detail linked to her documented cancer, whose site the sources do not record exactly</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C20</td><td>S — Synthetic histology, site, stage, mismatch repair status and course; the sources say she had cancer treated with a colostomy and call it colon cancer (R on the site). See sources.md.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

